WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.407
"Eliminating Heart Disease,
the Number One Cause of Death"

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.840
Heart disease is
the leading cause of death

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:10.720
in the United States,

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.440
and has been
our number one killer

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.120
every single year
for more than a century.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.080
Dr. William Clifford Roberts
published extensively

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.080
on the cause of our top killer.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.360
He was the Chief of Pathology

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.600
at the National Institutes
of Health for 30 years

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.480
before he headed up
Baylor University's

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.360
Heart and Vascular Institute.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.400
He authored more than
1,300 scientific publications,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.240
wrote more than a hundred
book chapters on cardiology,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.200
and was the editor-in-chief

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.440
of The American Journal
of Cardiology for 40 years.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.160
Well, what is the cause
of atherosclerosis?

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.400
Well, first of all,
didn't he mean causes?

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.680
I mean, there are
lots of things

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.200
that can increase
our risk of heart disease:

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.600
high blood pressure,
diabetes, cigarette smoking,

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.840
inactivity, obesity.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.400
But none of that matters,
he said,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.200
unless we have
high cholesterol.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.800
Atherosclerosis is
a cholesterol problem.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.040
Yes, these other factors
can amplify

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.520
the cholesterol damage,

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.920
but as long as cholesterol
levels are low enough,

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.040
heart disease remains rare.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.560
There's only one necessary
risk factor for atherosclerosis,

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.080
and that's elevated cholesterol
in the blood.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.280
How low does our cholesterol
have to be

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.440
to prevent and arrest
atherosclerotic plaques?

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.680
Ideally, our bad cholesterol,
the LDL,

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.400
should be under 70 milligrams
per deciliter,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.320
which is less than
1.8 millimole per liter.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.880
"If such a goal was created,
the great scourge

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:35.240
of the Western world would be
essentially eliminated."

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.400
So, we could put
a hundred million people

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.000
on a lifetime of sufficient
cholesterol-lowering drugs

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.080
or be what he called
a "pure vegetarian fruit eater,"

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.200
which is how he referred
to those eating whole food,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.840
plant-based diets.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.440
Now, if we put everyone
on drugs,

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.040
millions would suffer
side effects,

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.400
such as developing diabetes,

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.120
so, of course
a plant-based diet

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:56.400
"is the least expensive
and safest means

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.040
of achieving
the plaque-preventing LDL goal,

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.640
but few in the Western world
are willing

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.800
to live on the herbivore diet."

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.480
Because, according to, probably,

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.760
the most renowned cardiovascular
pathologist of all time,

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.000
the number one cause
of our number one killer

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.240
is elevated cholesterol,

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:16.160
which means the cause
of our number one killer

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.181
is not eating enough plants.

